# MAVI code owners.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern for a path, so a later rule
# replaces the owners of an earlier one rather than adding to them. Every
# rule in this file must therefore list @hariomahlawat. CODEOWNERS has no inline
# comments: only whole lines starting with '#' are comments, and a rule line
# containing '#' is refused.
# tools/verify_repo.py (check_code_owners) fails the repository contracts lane
# when a rule omits him, when a pattern has no owners (leaving paths unowned),
# when the first rule is not exactly "* @hariomahlawat", or when a second
# CODEOWNERS file (root or docs/) exists that GitHub would silently ignore.
#
# Ownership is separate from approval: branch rules on main do not require a
# code-owner review while @hariomahlawat is the only eligible reviewer,
# because GitHub does not let a pull request's author approve it.

*       @hariomahlawat
